10\\\\text{ kg}\\\\). \\n\\nNow, apply the same force \\\\(F = 20\\\\text{ N}\\\\) to the second object to find its acceleration \\\\(a_2\\\\):\\\\(a_2 = F / m_2 = 20\\\\text{ N} / 10\\\\text{ kg} = 2\\\\text{ m/s}^2\\\\).\",\"answers_hidden\":false},{\"question_id\":1532,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-06-15\",\"question_text\":\"A spaceship is traveling through space far from any gravitational influence. If its engines suddenly shut down, what will happen to the spaceship's motion according to Newton's First Law?\",\"choice_1\":\"It will immediately stop.\",\"choice_2\":\"It will gradually slow down and then stop.\",\"choice_3\":\"It will continue to move at a constant velocity.\",\"choice_4\":\"It will change direction.\",\"correct_option\":\"C\",\"difficulty_level\":\"Medium\",\"cognitive_level\":\"Applying\",\"learning_outcome\":\"Communication Proficiency\",\"question_type\":\"multiple choice\",\"school_type\":\"International\",\"subject\":\"Science\",\"year\":\"Year 12\",\"major\":null,\"course\":null,\"material\":null,\"semester\":null,\"company\":null,\"department\":null,\"job_role\":null,\"audience_type\":\"school\",\"mark\":5,\"time_seconds\":120,\"discriminating_factor\":null,\"status\":\"pending\",\"variables\":null,\"solution\":\"Newton's First Law (the Law of Inertia) states that an object in motion will stay in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced external force. In the vacuum of space, far from any gravitational fields or atmospheric resistance, there are no significant external forces to slow down or change the direction of the spaceship. Therefore, it will continue to move at a constant velocity.\",\"answers_hidden\":false}]}", "url": "http://localhost:6016/index.html", "timestamp": "2026-06-22T07:54:33.213Z"}
