2026-07-15 21:50:18,838 - INFO - main.py:197 - FRONTEND DEBUG: {"level": "log", "message": "fetchQuestions: Received response data: {\"total_count\":32,\"questions\":[{\"question_id\":1548,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-07-06\",\"question_text\":\"Which of Newton's laws describes the tendency of an object to resist changes in its state of motion, often referred to as inertia?\",\"choice_1\":\"A. Newton's First Law of Motion\",\"choice_2\":\"B. Newton's Second Law of Motion\",\"choice_3\":\"C. Newton's Third Law of Motion\",\"choice_4\":\"D. Newton's Law of Universal Gravitation\",\"correct_option\":\"A\",\"difficulty_level\":\"Easy\",\"cognitive_level\":\"Understanding\",\"learning_outcome\":\"Communication Proficiency\",\"question_type\":null,\"school_type\":\"International\",\"subject\":\"Science\",\"year\":\"Year 12\",\"major\":null,\"course\":null,\"material\":null,\"semester\":null,\"company\":null,\"department\":null,\"job_role\":null,\"audience_type\":\"school\",\"mark\":5,\"time_seconds\":120,\"discriminating_factor\":null,\"status\":\"pending\",\"variables\":null,\"solution\":\"Newton's First Law of Motion, also known as the law of inertia, states that an object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced force. This intrinsic property of matter to resist changes in its state of motion is called inertia, which is directly addressed by the first law. Newton's Second Law relates force, mass, and acceleration (\\\\(F=ma\\\\)), while Newton's Third Law describes action-reaction pairs. The Law of Universal Gravitation describes the attractive force between any two masses.\",\"answers_hidden\":false},{\"question_id\":1547,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-07-04\",\"question_text\":\"A rocket launches from Earth, accelerating upwards into space. Which of Newton's Laws primarily explains the origin of the propulsive force that causes the rocket to accelerate, and how does it relate to the expulsion of hot gases?\",\"choice_1\":\"A. Newton's First Law: The rocket overcomes its static inertia, and the gases are merely a byproduct of this process.\",\"choice_2\":\"B. Newton's Second Law: The net upward force on the rocket, caused by the expulsion of gases, directly results in its acceleration \\\\(F=ma\\\\).\",\"choice_3\":\"C. Newton's Third Law: The rocket expels hot gases downwards (action), and these gases exert an equal and opposite force upwards on the rocket (reaction), causing it to accelerate.\",\"choice_4\":\"D. Newton's Law of Universal Gravitation: The rocket's engines create a gravitational anomaly that repels it upwards, overcoming Earth's gravity.\",\"correct_option\":\"C\",\"difficulty_level\":\"Medium\",\"cognitive_level\":\"Applying\",\"learning_outcome\":\"Communication Proficiency\",\"question_type\":\"multiple choice\",\"school_type\":\"International\",\"subject\":\"Science\",\"year\":\"Year 12\",\"major\":null,\"course\":null,\"material\":null,\"semester\":null,\"company\":null,\"department\":null,\"job_role\":null,\"audience_type\":\"school\",\"mark\":5,\"time_seconds\":120,\"discriminating_factor\":null,\"status\":\"pending\",\"variables\":null,\"solution\":\"The propulsion of a rocket is a classic example of Newton's Third Law of Motion. Here's why:\\n\\n1.  **Newton's Third Law states:** For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.\\n2.  **Action:** The rocket engines burn fuel, expelling hot gases downwards with a certain force.\\n3.  **Reaction:** According to Newton's Third Law, these expelled gases exert an equal and opposite force upwards on the rocket itself.\\n4.  **Result:** This upward reaction force is the thrust that propels the rocket upwards, causing it to accelerate. While Newton's Second Law (\\\\(F=ma\\\\)) describes how this net force leads to acceleration, the *origin* of the propulsive force itself is explained by the action-reaction pair described by Newton's Third Law. Newton's First Law deals with inertia and the state of motion in the absence of net forces, and Newton's Law of Universal Gravitation describes the attractive force between masses, neither of which explains the propulsive mechanism.\",\"answers_hidden\":false},{\"question_id\":1546,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-07-01\",\"question_text\":\"Which city currently serves as the capital of Algeria, a North African country with a rich history?\",\"choice_1\":\"Oran\",\"choice_2\":\"Algiers\",\"choice_3\":\"Constantine\",\"choice_4\":\"Tlemcen\",\"correct_option\":\"B\",\"difficulty_level\":\"Easy\",\"cognitive_level\":\"Applying\",\"learning_outcome\":\"ability to identify places\",\"question_type\":\"multiple choice\",\"school_type\":\"Secondary\",\"subject\":\"History\",\"year\":\"Year 12\",\"major\":null,\"course\":null,\"material\":null,\"semester\":null,\"company\":null,\"department\":null,\"job_role\":null,\"audience_type\":\"school\",\"mark\":5,\"time_seconds\":120,\"discriminating_factor\":null,\"status\":\"pending\",\"variables\":null,\"solution\":\"The capital and largest city of Algeria is Algiers. It is located on the Mediterranean Sea and is the country's chief port and industrial center. The other cities listed are important Algerian cities but not the capital.\",\"answers_hidden\":false},{\"question_id\":1541,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-06-16\",\"question_text\":\"Which of the following statements correctly describes Kirchhoff's Current Law (KCL)?\",\"choice_1\":\"The sum of all voltages around any closed loop in a circuit is equal to zero.\",\"choice_2\":\"The algebraic sum of currents entering a junction (node) is equal to the algebraic sum of currents leaving that junction.\",\"choice_3\":\"The total resistance of a series circuit is the sum of individual resistances.\",\"choice_4\":\"The current flowing through a conductor between two points is directly proportional to the voltage across the two points.\",\"correct_option\":\"B\",\"difficulty_level\":\"Easy\",\"cognitive_level\":\"Remembering\",\"learning_outcome\":\"Communication Proficiency\",\"question_type\":\"multiple choice\",\"school_type\":\"Primary\",\"subject\":\"Science\",\"year\":\"Year 12\",\"major\":null,\"course\":null,\"material\":null,\"semester\":null,\"company\":null,\"department\":null,\"job_role\":null,\"audience_type\":\"school\",\"mark\":5,\"time_seconds\":120,\"discriminating_factor\":null,\"status\":\"pending\",\"variables\":null,\"solution\":\"Kirchhoff's Current Law (KCL) states that the algebraic sum of currents entering a junction (node) is equal to the algebraic sum of currents leaving that junction. This principle is based on the conservation of electric charge. Option A describes Kirchhoff's Voltage Law (KVL). Option C describes a property of series circuits, and Option D describes Ohm's Law.\",\"answers_hidden\":false},{\"question_id\":1540,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-06-16\",\"question_text\":\"[Dummy] Q1: Based on: dadc...\",\"choice_1\":\"1A\",\"choice_2\":\"1B\",\"choice_3\":\"1C\",\"choice_4\":\"1D\",\"correct_option\":\"A\",\"difficulty_level\":\"Medium\",\"cognitive_level\":\"Remembering\",\"learning_outcome\":\"Technical  Competence\",\"question_type\":\"multiple choice\",\"school_type\":\"Secondary\",\"subject\":\"Mathmatics\",\"year\":\"Year 4\",\"major\":null,\"course\":null,\"material\":null,\"semester\":null,\"company\":null,\"department\":null,\"job_role\":null,\"audience_type\":\"school\",\"mark\":5,\"time_seconds\":120,\"discriminating_factor\":null,\"status\":\"pending\",\"variables\":null,\"solution\":\"This is a dummy step-by-step solution.\",\"answers_hidden\":false},{\"question_id\":1539,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-06-15\",\"question_text\":\"A spacecraft is moving through deep space at a constant velocity of \\\\(10,000\\\\) m/s relative to a fixed star. If its engines are turned off, what can be inferred about the net external force acting on the spacecraft?\",\"choice_1\":\"The net external force is directed opposite to the spacecraft's motion, causing it to slow down gradually.\",\"choice_2\":\"The net external force is zero, allowing the spacecraft to continue its motion at a constant velocity according to Newton's First Law.\",\"choice_3\":\"The net external force is in the direction of the spacecraft's motion, maintaining its high speed.\",\"choice_4\":\"The net external force is constant and non-zero, as there is still gravitational pull from distant celestial bodies.\",\"correct_option\":\"B\",\"difficulty_level\":\"Medium\",\"cognitive_level\":\"Applying\",\"learning_outcome\":\"Communication Proficiency\",\"question_type\":\"multiple choice\",\"school_type\":\"International\",\"subject\":\"Science\",\"year\":\"Year 12\",\"major\":null,\"course\":null,\"material\":null,\"semester\":null,\"company\":null,\"department\":null,\"job_role\":null,\"audience_type\":\"school\",\"mark\":5,\"time_seconds\":120,\"discriminating_factor\":null,\"status\":\"pending\",\"variables\":null,\"solution\":\"According to Newton's First Law of Motion, an object in motion will stay in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced external force. Since the spacecraft is moving at a constant velocity (meaning zero acceleration) and its engines are off (implying no thrust), the net external force acting on it must be zero. Even in deep space, there might be minuscule gravitational forces, but for practical applications and the context of 'constant velocity' without engines, the net force is considered negligible or zero, allowing the constant velocity to persist. Therefore, option B is the correct inference.\",\"answers_hidden\":false},{\"question_id\":1538,\"author_creator\":\"TDM-AI-Engin\",\"date_created\":\"2026-06-15\",\"question_text\":\"The integral equation \\\\(y(